{"id":797,"slug":"jigoku","title":"Jigoku","year":1960,"country":"Japan","duration":101,"spine":352,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/797-jigoku","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/755cc14a06822abce0859f66f77ba87d/4ojfoQo0qFPOFyenaCA774vHWYBMWt_large.jpg","description":"Shocking, outrageous, and poetic, Jigoku (Hell, a.k.a. The Sinners of Hell) is the most innovative creation from Nobuo Nakagawa, the father of the Japanese horror film. After a young theology student flees a hit-and-run accident, he is plagued by both his own guilt-ridden conscience and a mysterious, diabolical doppelgänger. But all possible escape routes lead straight to hell—literally. In the gloriously gory final third of the film, Nakagawa offers up his vision of the underworld in a tour de force of torture and degradation. A striking departure from traditional Japanese ghost stories, Jigoku, with its truly eye-popping (and -gouging) imagery, created aftershocks that are still reverberating in contemporary world horror cinema. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Nobuo Nakagawa","slug":"nobuo-nakagawa"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Shigeru Amachi","role":"Shiro Shimizu","slug":"shigeru-amachi"},{"actor":"Utako Mitsuya","role":"Yukiko/Sachiko","slug":"utako-mitsuya"},{"actor":"Yoichi Numata","role":"Tamura","slug":"yoichi-numata"},{"actor":"Torahiko Nakamura","role":"Professor Yajima","slug":"torahiko-nakamura"},{"actor":"Fumiko Miyata","role":"Mrs. Yajima","slug":"fumiko-miyata"},{"actor":"Hiroshi Hayashi","role":"Gozo Shimizu","slug":"hiroshi-hayashi"},{"actor":"Kimie Tokudaiji","role":"Ito Shimizu","slug":"kimie-tokudaiji"},{"actor":"Akiko Yamashita","role":"Kinuko","slug":"akiko-yamashita"},{"actor":"Jun Otomo","role":"Ensai Taniguchi","slug":"jun-otomo"},{"actor":"Tomohiko Otani","role":"Dr. Kusama","slug":"tomohiko-otani"},{"actor":"Koichi Miya","role":"Journalist Akagawa","slug":"koichi-miya"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Nobuo Nakagawa","slug":"no